.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
app/debug_log.txt

# PyInstaller build directories
build/
dist/
*.spec
*.zip

# Claude Code local settings (per-machine, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Runtime artifacts written next to the app (per-machine, never distributed)
app/config.json
app/debug_log.prev.txt

# The Concierge's per-machine runtime state (v3.0). concierge_state.json names a
# pid and a port; concierge_key is one launch's API key; the memory note is the
# user's own text about their own machine. All four are in build_portable.py's
# RUNTIME_ARTIFACTS for the same reason they are here.
app/concierge_state.json
app/concierge_key
app/concierge_memory.txt
app/concierge_memory.prev.txt

# Downloaded weights: the Concierge GGUF (6.87 GB) and any bundled Whisper
# model. Excluded from the distribution zip by build_portable.py's EXCLUDED_DIRS
# and preserved across a reinstall by install.ps1 (design 10, Q27).
app/models/

# The bundled llama.cpp runtime, fetched by build_llama_runtime.py.
app/llama/

# NOTE: app/assets/concierge_kb.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is generated,
# but acceptance criterion v3-12 is "edit a source document without
# regenerating, run the L1 suite, the digest test fails and names the file" --
# which needs the pack present in a fresh clone to mean anything. Gate 2.5
# freezes and hashes it for the same reason.

# Test artifacts
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Build-cost records. Deliberately untracked: this repository is public, and the
# path is named here without any figures. To share this material, copy it out --
# a commit that adds it stays in a public repo's history even if a later commit
# deletes it.
docs/expenses/

# Spike scratch: llama.cpp binaries + GGUF weights (docs/ptt-v3-concierge/spike_prompt.md).
#
# Contents rather than the directory, so the two session-1 check scripts at the
# top level CAN be tracked. `concierge_design.md` section 5 names
# `spike/kv_persistence.py` as the mini-spike that decided which ready path
# ships, and `concierge_verification.md` section 4 says it is the check to re-run
# if a later llama.cpp build changes the answer -- a named check that is not in
# the repository is a dangling reference. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, hence `spike/*` and not `spike/`.
#
# Everything heavy stays out: spike/llama/ (640 MB), spike/models/ (7.4 GB),
# spike/out/ (raw results; the figures that matter are quoted in
# spike_results.md) and spike/checks/ (the original throwaway run).
spike/*
!spike/*.py

# The Concierge instruments' scratch (tests/tools/README.md). `.rig/` is the
# redirected APP_DIR a rig run writes its config.json, log and memory note into;
# `runs/` holds transcripts and scorecards. The figures that matter are quoted
# in model_qualification.md, the same way spike/out/ relates to spike_results.md.
tests/tools/.rig/
tests/tools/.probe/
tests/tools/runs/

# ...but the seeded logs are suite *data*, not artifacts, and `*.log` at the top
# of this file would otherwise swallow them. The diagnosis class is "given a
# seeded fake log, names the seeded cause": a scenario whose evidence is not in
# the repository is a check that cannot run on a fresh clone. Same argument as
# `!spike/*.py` above and as the note about concierge_kb.md.
!tests/tools/seeds/*.log
